sh":"0c60744201c9d725a7661f419cea2b378b1658af7d9864661c27dbb10f8081e4","event_uuid":"8fa4af82-2dd1-4954-972c-536c17052513","position":{"commit_sha":"6f61730c6f234c6d29a12daedbb6a974456a8d67","position":"1786680343502496001-8fa4af82-2dd1-4954-972c-536c17052513"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c6b813c2df9ec46d763f0a3e8e4b1dfa62ce691283d4c676f7ad461250e3612a","event_uuid":"07aac22e-0d2b-479c-9e5a-a4bf4440549a","position":{"commit_sha":"97998ea5a95efa058fa370f9131c00dccd2a17d5","position":"1786680362839207001-07aac22e-0d2b-479c-9e5a-a4bf4440549a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"97fb9246839c6d662753a3c4a8e7ae05dec531cebac05f425b58698511d80640","event_uuid":"e8b7b34c-fb00-4aac-bcb8-67a05a5efb40","position":{"commit_sha":"48bdafc1922125f90eb8528d5e0b5268e6066ea8","position":"1786680685748779001-e8b7b34c-fb00-4aac-bcb8-67a05a5efb40"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fccf769dd46d2d10c69cdce3bd290ad93570bbeaa0a31dfe14cfed6fb83c7e4c","event_uuid":"1c7c1f1a-614c-4c72-8bc5-f9387833081f","position":{"commit_sha":"e8e4508379a12a6b53f5100bed4f2c00bdfad988","position":"1786680688125775001-1c7c1f1a-614c-4c72-8bc5-f9387833081f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CURRENT BEHAVIOR REPORT (operator-observed, 2026-08-13, post-1739-merge):\n\nA third occurrence of the restartable-lock pathology, AFTER 1739 merged. An orphaned compactor (PPID 1) spawned from a temporary `wt-close` worktree ran 12+ minutes and held the shared store lock for 5+ minutes, blocking a queued transactional ticket write. The operator gracefully terminated only its isolated process group so the queued write could finish — the same manual-kill remedy this ticket exists to make unnecessary.\n\nMechanism (why old code ran after the fix merged): the `wt-close` worktree's close operations ran via the MAIN checkout's venv (`/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.venv`, an editable install of the main checkout's working tree), and the main checkout had not been advanced to the merged 1739. The operation-linked trigger therefore detached a sweep executing the PRE-1739 per-ticket history-walk code. Any environment whose rebar build predates 50cc45f0d1 will keep reproducing this until its checkout/install advances — the fix's deployment lags its merge wherever editable installs track stale checkouts.\n\nImplications for this ticket's plan: (1) reinforces the core case — all three incidents were resolved by a human manually identifying and killing a holder the tooling described only as a bare pid; the `op=compact-sweep` stamp and stated-remedy error text would have made each self-service; (2) consider the stamp carrying the code version/commit of the holder, so an operator can see at a glance that a holder is running superseded code.","timestamp":1786663804659611001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"[operator-attested] Gate + CI evidence for the two external-evidence acceptance criteria.\n\nLocal gate set (worktree /Users/joeoakhart/camerashy-land, base origin/main 4c4225c3dd + this change):\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_lock_holder_labelling.py -q` -> 11 passed.\n- Related lock suite (test_lock_holder_labelling, test_lock_timeout_names_holder_7084,\n  test_lock_stale_reclaim, test_lock_age_ceiling, test_lock_container_recreate,\n  test_write_lock_busy_probe_7084, test_lock_retry_zebrafish) -> 91 passed.\n- `make lint` -> ruff check + ruff format --check + zizmor + actionlint all clean, EXIT 0.\n- `make typecheck` -> mypy \"Success: no issues found in 529 source files\", EXIT 0.\n\nCI's pytest tiers (Gerrit change 1758, GitHub Actions run 31766247222 \"main Gerrit Verified Gate\"):\n- pytest (ubuntu-latest py3.11/py3.12/py3.13) passed; pytest (macos-latest py3.13) passed;\n  lint + type-check passed; build-and-test suite, optionality, artifact-probe, golden-path,\n  verify-identity, mutation shards, eval-discipline all green.\n- Gerrit gates: LLM-Review +1 (rebar code review PASS, 1 non-blocking advisory) AND Verified +1.\n  Change submitted -> status MERGED (Rebase-If-Necessary); unresolved_comment_count = 0.\n- Run: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/31766247222\n- Change: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1758","timestamp":1786680343502496001}],"created_at":1786655926821684001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"472b32a0-e253-4165-8562-53c946335a67","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0d15-59a4-e140-444b"},{"link_uuid":"8e49a48e-72be-4a5a-a7fc-3fdba09ab300","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f53e-7a08-212a-4fdc"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nWhen a compaction sweep holds the store write lock, a blocked session cannot tell what is\nholding it or whether interrupting it is safe. Both facts are already known to the code and\nneither reaches the operator.\n\nLive incident 2026-08-13 (`vigilant-erasable-pony`): a sweep held\n`.tickets-tracker/.ticket-write.lock` for 24+ minutes at 0.0% CPU. The blocked session saw:\n\n    flock: could not acquire lock after 181s (holder: host=... pid=... held=47s)\n\nA bare pid. Identifying it as compaction required `lsof`/`ps`. The blast radius is host-wide\nacross worktrees, so \"check your own checkout\" does not help.\n\nThe answer is already documented: `compact_trigger.run_sweep` guarantees \"a skipped sweep is a\nno-op for correctness (the events stay live and the next trigger folds them)\". An operator\nholding that guarantee can safely SIGTERM the holder. Looking at an unattributed pid, the safe\nresponse is to wait — which is exactly wrong here. One sweep was killed manually (pid 98440,\n26 minutes) to unblock three agents.\n\n## Approach\nSay what the holder is, and that it is interruptible — at the two places a blocked writer\nalready looks.\n\n**1. Label the lock holder, ambiently.** `lock_owner._owner_stamp` writes the v2 ownership line\n(`rebar-lock v2 host=... ns=... pid=... start=...`) that `describe_lock_holder` renders into\nevery `LockTimeout`. That stamp is written by `_acquire_mkdir` (`lock.py`), reached only through\n`lock.acquire`. Add an optional operation label so the timeout reads\n`... pid=98440 held=181s op=compact-sweep` instead of a bare pid.\n\nThe label must reach `_owner_stamp` WITHOUT editing the acquisition call site: the sweep's\nstore-write-lock acquisition is `lock.acquire()` in `compact_txn._compact_locked`\n(`compact_txn.py:358`), invoked per ticket, and `compact_txn.py` is deliberately OUT of scope\n(it carries the just-landed sweep-perf change `mesodermic-vaporish-seaslug` and must not be\nre-touched). The satisfying mechanism is an AMBIENT label, not a new `acquire` parameter:\n\n- `lock_owner.py` gains a process/thread-local label — a `contextvars.ContextVar` plus an\n  `operation_label(label)` context manager that sets it on enter and resets on exit.\n  `_owner_stamp()` reads that contextvar and, when set, appends a single colon-free `op=<label>`\n  field. Unset (every ordinary writer) ⇒ the stamp is byte-identical to today's.\n- The sweep sets that contextvar around its whole body at its two entry points\n  (`compact_trigger.run_sweep`, `compact.py`'s sweep loop). Every `lock.acquire` beneath that\n  `with` block — including the per-ticket `lock.acquire()` inside `_compact_locked`, which this\n  ticket does NOT modify — writes its stamp with `op=compact-sweep`. Data flow: sweep-entry →\n  contextvar → `_owner_stamp`; the label reaches the stamp ambiently and `compact_txn.py` needs\n  no change. `contextvars` is the right carrier because the label is read synchronously in the\n  same process/thread that later calls `acquire`: the sweep folds inline (`_sweep_one_ticket` →\n  `compact_cli` → `_compact_locked`), so the ambient value is in scope at the acquisition.\n\nThe v2 format's forward-compat contract is preserved exactly: the line is COLON-FREE so an older\nrebar splitting on `host, sep, pid = stamp.partition(\":\")` finds no separator and declines to\nact (bug castoff-tigerseye-ammonite). A new `key=value` field keeps that (the label value is\nsanitized to strip any `:`, `=`, or whitespace, staying one colon-free token), and\n`_parse_v2_stamp` already ignores unknown fields. The label is descriptive only —\n`_stamp_is_stale` / `stamped_file_is_stale` never read `op=`, so reclamation is unaffected.\n\n**2. State the remedy in the error.** `describe_lock_holder` renders the `op=` field into the\nholder string; `LockTimeout` recognises the known interruptible label (`compact-sweep`) in that\nstring and appends a remedy line — that the holder is a compaction sweep, interrupting it loses\nno data, and the next trigger re-folds. An ordinary (unlabelled) holder gets no remedy line.\n\nDeliberately NOT here: auto-killing a long sweep. That is a separate pre-emption policy; the\nreported incidents were all resolved by a human given the right information. Inform first.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_store/lock_owner.py` — an ambient operation-label contextvar + `operation_label`\n  context manager; `_owner_stamp` appends an optional colon-free `op=` field (sanitized to one\n  token) when set; a helper mapping a known interruptible label to its remedy text. Never\n  consulted by staleness logic.\n- `src/rebar/_store/lock.py` — render the `op=` label in `describe_lock_holder`; extend the\n  `LockTimeout` message with the safe-to-interrupt remedy when the holder string names a known\n  interruptible operation.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py` — wrap `run_sweep`'s body in\n  `lock_owner.operation_label(\"compact-sweep\")` (the ambient carrier — not an edit to any\n  acquisition call), so the store-lock acquisitions it drives via `_compact_locked` stamp it.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact.py` — wrap the sweep loop (`compact_all_cli`/`_run_sweep`) in the\n  same `operation_label(\"compact-sweep\")`, so a direct `rebar compact-all` is also labelled.\n- `tests/unit/test_lock_holder_labelling.py` — new tests.\n\nPortability: the mechanism is a colon-free `key=value` field in the lock stamp file plus an\nin-process `contextvars` label — no CI provider, external service, or platform facility — so it\nworks identically anywhere rebar runs, with or without CI.\n\n## Testing\n- A labelled holder appears in `describe_lock_holder` and in the `LockTimeout` message\n  (asserting `op=compact-sweep`, not only a pid).\n- The remedy text is PRESENT for a labelled optional holder, ABSENT for an ordinary writer.\n- An UNLABELLED holder renders byte-identically to today's `describe_lock_holder` output.\n- The stamp stays colon-free with the label; a label containing `:`/`=`/whitespace is sanitized.\n- `_parse_v2_stamp` accepts a stamp carrying an unknown extra field (forward compat).\n- Reclamation is label-blind: a labelled and unlabelled stale lock adjudicate identically.\n- End to end: with `operation_label(\"compact-sweep\")` active, a real `lock.acquire` writes an\n  owner stamp carrying the label — the ambient contextvar reaches `_owner_stamp` through the\n  actual acquisition path `_compact_locked` uses.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A blocked writer's `LockTimeout` names the holder as a compaction sweep — a test asserts\n      the message contains the operation label rather than only a pid.\n- [x] The remedy text (safe, lossless) is present for a labelled optional holder — a test\n      asserts it.\n- [x] The remedy text is absent for an ordinary writer — a test asserts it.\n- [x] An unlabelled holder's rendering is byte-identical to today's — a test pins the format.\n- [x] The stamp remains colon-free with a label present — a test asserts it.\n- [x] `_parse_v2_stamp` ignores an unknown extra field — a test asserts it.\n- [x] Staleness/reclamation ignore the label — a test asserts a labelled and unlabelled stale\n      lock adjudicate identically.\n- [x] The label reaches the stamp through the real acquisition path via the ambient contextvar —\n      a test drives `lock.acquire` under `operation_label(...)` and asserts the written stamp\n      carries `op=compact-sweep`.\n- [x] The full local gate set passes. [operator-attested]\n- [x] CI's pytest tiers pass. [operator-attested]","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/lock_owner.py","reason":"optional colon-free op= field in the v2 ownership stamp, ignored by older readers and never consulted by staleness logic"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/lock.py","reason":"render the operation label in describe_lock_holder and add the safe-to-interrupt remedy to LockTimeout for labelled optional holders"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py","reason":"label the sweep worker lock acquisitions"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact.py","reason":"label the sweep loop lock acquisitions"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_lock_holder_labelling.py","reason":"tests for labelled and unlabelled rendering, the colon-free forward-compat contract, and reclamation being label-blind"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","f53e-7a08-212a-4fdc"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e8b7b34c-fb00-4aac-bcb8-67a05a5efb40","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"301d-0769-ed02-42f6","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Lock timeouts name a bare pid, not the compaction sweep holding it","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["856f4819-a4a0-4e39-a686-bbdf27c218fe","db06f17b-23e2-4ed1-83c2-dc5472af0375","8854d6b0-9b13-4239-97ed-3e11e2b139a2","b48bee7e-5841-498a-b5b0-066c5d924ae6","26af1e92-c6b7-414d-97eb-ce5776c1b00c","92998f6b-699a-4f56-bfa8-3e7a8f4488e3","8e49a48e-72be-4a5a-a7fc-3fdba09ab300","496ed58e-fb7b-4196-89c5-3f9c84db6c13","8fa4af82-2dd1-4954-972c-536c17052513","07aac22e-0d2b-479c-9e5a-a4bf4440549a","e8b7b34c-fb00-4aac-bcb8-67a05a5efb40","1c7c1f1a-614c-4c72-8bc5-f9387833081f"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786688861523905674,"uuid":"b4f08994-57bd-40b3-9c3f-451d72794732"}